{"id": "EUVD-2026-97431", "enisaUuid": "bc440ecd-0a5f-3b97-be27-304d638e6c2d", "description": "SGLang through 0.5.21 contains an unbounded memory allocation vulnerability that allows unauthenticated remote attackers to exhaust memory by uploading oversized files to /v1/audio/transcriptions. Attackers can send concurrent large multipart uploads, which are fully read into memory before validation, to crash the HTTP/tokenizer worker and deny service.", "datePublished": "2026-10-12T14:04:29", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-13T16:57:32", "baseScore": 8.7, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/issues/43709", "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/v0.5.21/python/sglang/srt/entrypoints/http_server.py#L1847-L1871", "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/sglang-through-0.5.21-memory-exhaustion-dos-via-v1-audio-transcriptions-upload"], "aliases": ["GHSA-4fxq-6r94-mchm", "CVE-2026-109225"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.43, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "812b9d66-2639-35ca-81bd-25f81ae6545a", "product": {"name": "sglang", "vendor": {"name": "sgl-project"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22640.5.21"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "603f835d-f667-3ff3-8f15-d11f95efbe29", "vendor": {"name": "sgl-project"}}], "isExploited": false}